  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 20,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "THE WEAVE. One piece of tissue with two ways in. A noise field (patches, coverage 0.4) picks scattered patches of the cells for channel A; a second field with a different seed picks other patches for channel B. The two sets are woven through each other and share their neighbours. There are no areas and no hierarchy. The only plastic pathway is the recurrence.",
    "width": 340,
    "near": ""
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 560,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "Dense flat recurrence, with the triplet and short-term terms on, after Pokorny et al. 2019, where spike timing plasticity alone associates two assemblies in a recurrent network of about this size.",
    "width": 340,
    "near": ""
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 830,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "Training blocks: channel A alone for 20 simulated minutes, then B alone for 20, then both together for 80. The one-channel probes run unchanged through every block.",
    "width": 340,
    "near": ""
   },
   "inputs": []
